# Build context hygiene for `docker build` (Phase8 J + Phase20 PD-SEC-07).
# The frontend is built INSIDE the image (stage 1 compiles it), so local
# build artifacts/caches must never enter the context.
#
# PD-SEC-07: `.env` and every `.env.*` variant are git-ignored AND excluded
# from the Docker build context. Even when a Dockerfile step never copies them
# into the final image, an unexcluded `.env` would still be sent to a remote
# daemon / remote builder / build cache. `.env.example` (the documented
# example) stays in the context. Operator secrets ONLY ever live in
# operator-local `.env` / environment, never in the build context.

# VCS / governance
.git
.gitignore
.rad

# Local dev environments / tooling
.venv
venv
env
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
opencode.json
.opencode
.claude
.codex
.cursor
.ollama

# -------- Phase 20 PD-SEC-07: operator secrets never reach the builder ------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs (local/runtime; never part of the image)
logs/
*.log

# Local temp dirs
tmp/
temp/

# Node (built inside the image; local copies are dev-only)
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
e2e/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Runtime databases — persisted in the /data volume, never baked in
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
procedural_detective.db

# QA / audit artifacts
e2e/artifacts
tests/__pycache__
screenshots/generated

# Local documents that are not part of the runtime image
ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md
BENCHMARKS.md
DECISIONS.md
DEFECTS.md
PACKAGE_CONTENTS.md
POC_REPORT.md
Phase*.md
PhaseRisks.md
REQUIREMENTS.md

# Packaging leftovers
*.egg-info
build
dist